text:
@Mortorosso Bruh.
I was just gonna say, I love how this kind of tracks are made. You set up some initial parameters, and then it just goes. 
It's like it's alive.

@PolarityAmbient amazing! 

could i ask btw whats the general method for doing those "animal sounds" in the ambiance ? they completely teleport me to another reality

 and one last thing, i dont meant to sound like i am riding a high horse but please dont post with an AI cover, your work (this one especially omg) deserves better representation for such depth. I am going to listen to it either way, but i know that if i didn't know your work and saw an ai cover, I (and countless other people) would just skip it without even giving a listen, so using an ai cover at the very least will be like shooting yourself in the foot, i have no doubt you can get an amazing cover for 10-50 bucks in fiverr for example, and its also a fun experience talking to another artist and discussing your vision

@JavisJones3DCG I'm just FurryWrecker911. Used to be active on the Foundry Forums a little bit years ago, but these days I'm more active in the fire alarm industry since 3D art jobs became harder and harder. I still do digital drawings and upload to DeviantArt when I do make things. 

It's a shame that Modo was axed. I was trained in Maya but I got hooked on Modo through my old training software job in the 2010s (boss was a diehard fan of Lightwave eons ago). Delivered on 14 different plane and ship trainers for the Navy using Modo, Substance, and Unity. Great times. I never let it go, even after Blender took off years later. I still use my 17.1 copy every now and then to make small personal projects.

I'm just so much faster with it than anything else because it prioritized fewer clicks and key strokes for basic actions like extruding, bridging, etc. Blender, Maya, Max, they all make you play Dance Dance Revolution with the keyboard for every command. lol
